chapters.bodyZh:
栈、队列和双端队列在 STL 里各有现成的类型。它们的接口很像，但有几个细节和 Python、Java 都不一样，最典型的是 `pop()` 不返回值。

## stack：后进先出

```cpp
stack<int> st;
st.push(1);
st.push(2);
st.top();      // 2：看栈顶，不删除
st.pop();      // 删除栈顶，返回 void
st.empty(); st.size();
```

`int x = st.pop();` 编译不过。要先 `st.top()` 取值，再 `st.pop()` 删除。对空栈调用 `top()` 或 `pop()` 不会抛异常，而是未定义行为，所以先判断 `empty()`。

`vector` 也能当栈用：`push_back`、`back`、`pop_back`。它还能随时遍历和按下标访问，很多人刷题时更喜欢直接用 `vector`。

## queue：先进先出

```cpp
queue<int> q;
q.push(1);     // 从队尾进
q.front();     // 队头
q.back();      // 队尾
q.pop();       // 删除队头，同样返回 void
```

BFS 的标准写法：

```cpp
queue<int> q;
q.push(start);
seen[start] = true;
while (!q.empty()) {
    int u = q.front();
    q.pop();
    for (int v : adj[u])
        if (!seen[v]) { seen[v] = true; q.push(v); }
}
```

入队时就标记 `seen`，而不是出队时才标记，否则同一个点可能被放进队列很多次。

`stack` 和 `queue` 都是"适配器"：它们包着一个底层容器，只开放受限的接口，不能用范围 for 遍历，也没有 `clear()`。要清空可以直接赋一个新对象：`q = queue<int>();`。

## deque：两头都能进出

`deque` 两端插入和删除都是 O(1)，还支持 `d[i]` 随机访问：

```cpp
deque<int> d;
d.push_back(x); d.push_front(x);
d.pop_back(); d.pop_front();
d.front(); d.back(); d[i];
```

滑动窗口里常用的"单调队列"就建立在 `deque` 上：新元素从队尾进，同时从队尾弹出所有比它差的元素，过期的元素从队头弹出。`queue` 的默认底层容器也是 `deque`。

## 例子：有效的括号

遇到左括号入栈，遇到右括号就和栈顶配对。

```cpp run
#include <deque>
#include <iostream>
#include <queue>
#include <stack>
#include <string>
using namespace std;

bool isValid(const string& s) {
    stack<char> st;
    for (char c : s) {
        if (c == '(' || c == '[' || c == '{') {
            st.push(c);
            continue;
        }
        if (st.empty()) return false;   // 右括号多了
        char open = st.top();
        st.pop();
        if ((c == ')' && open != '(') || (c == ']' && open != '[') || (c == '}' && open != '{')) return false;
    }
    return st.empty();                   // 左括号多了
}

int main() {
    cout << isValid("([]{})") << isValid("(]") << isValid("((") << '\n';

    queue<int> q;
    for (int x : {1, 2, 3}) q.push(x);
    q.pop();
    cout << q.front() << ' ' << q.back() << ' ' << q.size() << '\n';

    deque<int> d = {2, 3};
    d.push_front(1);
    d.push_back(4);
    cout << d[0] << ' ' << d[3] << ' ' << d.size() << '\n';
}
```

```text
100
2 3 2
1 4 4
```

## 常见错误

- 写 `int x = st.pop();`。C++ 的 `pop()` 只删除不返回。
- 对空的 `stack`、`queue` 调用 `top()`、`front()`、`pop()`，程序不会报错，只会出现诡异结果或崩溃。
- BFS 出队时才标记已访问，导致同一个点重复入队，最坏情况下内存和时间都会爆掉。
- 想用范围 for 遍历 `stack` 或 `queue`。需要遍历时改用 `vector` 或 `deque`。

chapters.bodyEn:
The STL has a ready-made type for stacks, queues and double-ended queues. Their interfaces look alike, and a few details differ from Python and Java, most famously that `pop()` returns nothing.

## stack: last in, first out

```cpp
stack<int> st;
st.push(1);
st.push(2);
st.top();      // 2: look at the top without removing it
st.pop();      // remove the top; returns void
st.empty(); st.size();
```

`int x = st.pop();` does not compile. Read the value with `st.top()` first, then remove it with `st.pop()`. Calling `top()` or `pop()` on an empty stack throws nothing; it is undefined behavior, so check `empty()` first.

A `vector` works as a stack too: `push_back`, `back`, `pop_back`. It can also be iterated and indexed at any time, so many people simply use a `vector`.

## queue: first in, first out

```cpp
queue<int> q;
q.push(1);     // enter at the back
q.front();     // the front
q.back();      // the back
q.pop();       // remove the front; also returns void
```

The standard BFS loop:

```cpp
queue<int> q;
q.push(start);
seen[start] = true;
while (!q.empty()) {
    int u = q.front();
    q.pop();
    for (int v : adj[u])
        if (!seen[v]) { seen[v] = true; q.push(v); }
}
```

Mark `seen` when a node enters the queue, not when it leaves, or the same node can be queued many times.

`stack` and `queue` are adaptors: they wrap another container and expose a narrow interface. You cannot range-for over them and they have no `clear()`. To empty one, assign a fresh object: `q = queue<int>();`.

## deque: in and out at both ends

A `deque` inserts and removes at either end in O(1) and still supports `d[i]`:

```cpp
deque<int> d;
d.push_back(x); d.push_front(x);
d.pop_back(); d.pop_front();
d.front(); d.back(); d[i];
```

The monotonic queue used in sliding-window problems is built on a `deque`: a new element enters at the back after popping every worse element from the back, and expired elements leave from the front. `queue` uses a `deque` underneath by default.

## Example: valid parentheses

Push opening brackets; match each closing bracket against the top of the stack.

```cpp run
#include <deque>
#include <iostream>
#include <queue>
#include <stack>
#include <string>
using namespace std;

bool isValid(const string& s) {
    stack<char> st;
    for (char c : s) {
        if (c == '(' || c == '[' || c == '{') {
            st.push(c);
            continue;
        }
        if (st.empty()) return false;   // too many closing brackets
        char open = st.top();
        st.pop();
        if ((c == ')' && open != '(') || (c == ']' && open != '[') || (c == '}' && open != '{')) return false;
    }
    return st.empty();                   // too many opening brackets
}

int main() {
    cout << isValid("([]{})") << isValid("(]") << isValid("((") << '\n';

    queue<int> q;
    for (int x : {1, 2, 3}) q.push(x);
    q.pop();
    cout << q.front() << ' ' << q.back() << ' ' << q.size() << '\n';

    deque<int> d = {2, 3};
    d.push_front(1);
    d.push_back(4);
    cout << d[0] << ' ' << d[3] << ' ' << d.size() << '\n';
}
```

```text
100
2 3 2
1 4 4
```

## Common mistakes

- Writing `int x = st.pop();`. In C++, `pop()` removes and returns nothing.
- Calling `top()`, `front()` or `pop()` on an empty `stack` or `queue`: no error, just strange results or a crash.
- Marking BFS nodes as visited when they leave the queue, so a node is queued repeatedly and time and memory blow up.
- Trying to range-for over a `stack` or `queue`. Use a `vector` or `deque` when you need to iterate.

chapters.bodyZh:
`priority_queue` 是 C++ 的堆。堆的原理见"Big-O 与数据结构速成课"的堆一课，这里讲用法，以及最容易写反的比较器。

## 默认是最大堆

和 Python 的 `heapq` 相反，`priority_queue<int>` 默认**堆顶是最大值**：

```cpp
priority_queue<int> pq;
pq.push(3); pq.push(1); pq.push(4);
pq.top();      // 4，O(1)
pq.pop();      // 删除堆顶，O(log n)，返回 void
```

最小堆要写出全部三个模板参数：

```cpp
priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> minq;
```

已经有一个数组时，用区间构造一次建好堆，是 O(n)，比逐个 `push` 的 O(n log n) 快：

```cpp
priority_queue<int> pq(a.begin(), a.end());
```

## pair 和 tuple 按字典序比较

`priority_queue<pair<int, int>>` 先比 `first`，相等再比 `second`，堆顶是最大的那对。Dijkstra 常写成最小堆加 `{距离, 结点}`：

```cpp
priority_queue<pair<long long, int>, vector<pair<long long, int>>, greater<>> pq;
pq.push({0, src});
while (!pq.empty()) {
    auto [d, u] = pq.top();
    pq.pop();
    if (d > dist[u]) continue;   // 过期的记录，跳过
    ...
}
```

`priority_queue` 不支持修改堆里某个元素的优先级。常见做法是直接再放一条新记录，弹出旧记录时发现它已经过期就跳过，这叫"懒删除"。

## 自定义比较器：方向和直觉相反

比较器 `cmp(a, b)` 返回 `true` 表示 **a 的优先级更低，应该排在 b 后面出堆**。所以：

- `less<T>`（`a < b`）：大的先出，最大堆，也就是默认行为。
- `greater<T>`（`a > b`）：小的先出，最小堆。

写结构体或 lambda 时同理：想让小的先出，比较器就写 `a.x > b.x`。

```cpp run
#include <iostream>
#include <queue>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

struct Task {
    int priority;
    string name;
};

int main() {
    // later(a, b) 为 true 表示 a 比 b 晚出堆：数字大的晚出，所以数字小的先出
    auto later = [](const Task& a, const Task& b) { return a.priority > b.priority; };
    priority_queue<Task, vector<Task>, decltype(later)> pq(later);
    pq.push({3, "deploy"});
    pq.push({1, "fix bug"});
    pq.push({2, "review"});
    while (!pq.empty()) {
        cout << pq.top().priority << ' ' << pq.top().name << '\n';
        pq.pop();
    }
}
```

```text
1 fix bug
2 review
3 deploy
```

## 例子：第 K 大的元素、最后一块石头

求第 k 大：维护一个大小为 k 的最小堆，里面始终是目前最大的 k 个数，堆顶就是第 k 大，时间 O(n log k)。石头问题每次取最重的两块，正好用最大堆。

```cpp run
#include <iostream>
#include <queue>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

int findKthLargest(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
    priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> h;   // 最大的 k 个数组成的最小堆
    for (int x : nums) {
        h.push(x);
        if ((int)h.size() > k) h.pop();                 // 弹出最小的
    }
    return h.top();
}

int lastStoneWeight(vector<int>& stones) {
    priority_queue<int> h(stones.begin(), stones.end());   // 最大堆，O(n) 建堆
    while (h.size() > 1) {
        int y = h.top(); h.pop();
        int x = h.top(); h.pop();
        if (y != x) h.push(y - x);
    }
    return h.empty() ? 0 : h.top();
}

int main() {
    vector<int> a = {3, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4};
    cout << findKthLargest(a, 2) << '\n';
    vector<int> s = {2, 7, 4, 1, 8, 1};
    cout << lastStoneWeight(s) << '\n';
}
```

```text
5
1
```

## 常见错误

- 以为 `priority_queue<int>` 是最小堆。默认是最大堆，最小堆要写 `greater<int>`。
- 自定义比较器写反，得到的顺序和预期正好相反。记住：返回 `true` 的那一方后出堆。
- 想遍历堆或者修改堆里的元素。`priority_queue` 只能看到堆顶；要修改优先级，就放一条新记录，再懒删除旧记录。
- 对空堆调用 `top()`。

chapters.bodyEn:
`priority_queue` is the C++ heap. How heaps work is covered in the Big-O course's heap chapter; this one is about usage and the comparator, which is the part people most often write backwards.

## A max-heap by default

The opposite of Python's `heapq`: `priority_queue<int>` keeps the **largest value on top**:

```cpp
priority_queue<int> pq;
pq.push(3); pq.push(1); pq.push(4);
pq.top();      // 4, O(1)
pq.pop();      // remove the top, O(log n); returns void
```

A min-heap needs all three template arguments:

```cpp
priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> minq;
```

When you already have the values, building from a range is O(n), faster than n pushes at O(n log n):

```cpp
priority_queue<int> pq(a.begin(), a.end());
```

## pairs and tuples compare lexicographically

`priority_queue<pair<int, int>>` compares `first`, then `second` on a tie, and the largest pair is on top. Dijkstra is usually a min-heap of `{distance, node}`:

```cpp
priority_queue<pair<long long, int>, vector<pair<long long, int>>, greater<>> pq;
pq.push({0, src});
while (!pq.empty()) {
    auto [d, u] = pq.top();
    pq.pop();
    if (d > dist[u]) continue;   // a stale entry: skip it
    ...
}
```

A `priority_queue` cannot change the priority of an element already inside. The usual trick is to push a new entry and skip the old one when it surfaces and turns out stale; this is called lazy deletion.

## Custom comparators run backwards

A comparator `cmp(a, b)` returns `true` when **a has lower priority and should leave the heap after b**. So:

- `less<T>` (`a < b`): larger values leave first, a max-heap, the default.
- `greater<T>` (`a > b`): smaller values leave first, a min-heap.

The same goes for structs and lambdas: to pop the smallest first, the comparator says `a.x > b.x`.

```cpp run
#include <iostream>
#include <queue>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

struct Task {
    int priority;
    string name;
};

int main() {
    // later(a, b) is true when a leaves after b: larger numbers wait, so the smallest comes out first
    auto later = [](const Task& a, const Task& b) { return a.priority > b.priority; };
    priority_queue<Task, vector<Task>, decltype(later)> pq(later);
    pq.push({3, "deploy"});
    pq.push({1, "fix bug"});
    pq.push({2, "review"});
    while (!pq.empty()) {
        cout << pq.top().priority << ' ' << pq.top().name << '\n';
        pq.pop();
    }
}
```

```text
1 fix bug
2 review
3 deploy
```

## Examples: the k-th largest element and the last stone

For the k-th largest, keep a min-heap of size k holding the k largest values so far; its top is the answer, in O(n log k). The stone problem smashes the two heaviest stones each round, a natural max-heap.

```cpp run
#include <iostream>
#include <queue>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

int findKthLargest(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
    priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> h;   // a min-heap of the k largest values
    for (int x : nums) {
        h.push(x);
        if ((int)h.size() > k) h.pop();                 // drop the smallest
    }
    return h.top();
}

int lastStoneWeight(vector<int>& stones) {
    priority_queue<int> h(stones.begin(), stones.end());   // a max-heap, built in O(n)
    while (h.size() > 1) {
        int y = h.top(); h.pop();
        int x = h.top(); h.pop();
        if (y != x) h.push(y - x);
    }
    return h.empty() ? 0 : h.top();
}

int main() {
    vector<int> a = {3, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4};
    cout << findKthLargest(a, 2) << '\n';
    vector<int> s = {2, 7, 4, 1, 8, 1};
    cout << lastStoneWeight(s) << '\n';
}
```

```text
5
1
```

## Common mistakes

- Assuming `priority_queue<int>` is a min-heap. It is a max-heap; a min-heap needs `greater<int>`.
- Writing the custom comparator backwards and getting exactly the reverse order. The side that returns `true` leaves later.
- Trying to iterate over the heap or change an element inside it. Only the top is visible; to change a priority, push a new entry and lazily skip the old one.
- Calling `top()` on an empty heap.

chapters.bodyZh:
`unordered_map` 和 `unordered_set` 是哈希表：查找、插入、删除平均 O(1)，最坏 O(n)，元素**没有顺序**。计数、判重、"见过没有"这类需求用它们；需要有序或者要找前驱、后继时，用上一课的 `set` 和 `map`。

## 基本用法

```cpp
unordered_map<int, int> cnt;
for (int x : nums) cnt[x]++;          // 键不存在时从 0 开始
cnt.count(7);                          // 0 或 1
auto it = cnt.find(7);                 // 找到后用 it->first、it->second
if (it != cnt.end()) ...
cnt.erase(7);

unordered_set<string> seen;
seen.insert("a");
if (seen.count("a")) ...
```

`[]` 会插入默认值，这一点和 `map` 一样。只查询时用 `find` 或 `count`。`find` 返回迭代器，找到后可以直接用 `it->second`，避免再查一次。

## 选 map 还是 unordered_map

| | `map` | `unordered_map` |
|---|---|---|
| 底层 | 红黑树 | 哈希表 |
| 查找、插入 | O(log n) | 平均 O(1)，最坏 O(n) |
| 遍历顺序 | 按键有序 | 不确定 |
| 键的要求 | 能用 `<` 比较 | 要有哈希函数 |

面试里默认用 `unordered_map`。需要按键有序输出、需要 `lower_bound`，或者键是 `pair`、`vector` 这类没有默认哈希的类型时，用 `map`。

## pair 当键

标准库没有给 `pair` 提供哈希，`unordered_set<pair<int, int>>` 编译不过。三种办法：

1. 改用 `set<pair<int, int>>`，多一个 log。
2. 把两个数编码成一个整数，例如网格坐标写成 `r * cols + c`。
3. 自己写一个哈希函数（见下面的程序）。

## 例子：两数之和、字母异位词分组、存在重复元素 II

```cpp run
#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <unordered_set>
#include <utility>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

vector<int> twoSum(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
    unordered_map<int, int> seen;              // 值 -> 下标
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)nums.size(); i++) {
        auto it = seen.find(target - nums[i]);
        if (it != seen.end()) return {it->second, i};
        seen[nums[i]] = i;
    }
    return {};
}

vector<vector<string>> groupAnagrams(vector<string>& strs) {
    unordered_map<string, vector<string>> groups;
    for (const string& w : strs) {
        string key = w;
        sort(key.begin(), key.end());          // 排序后的字母当键
        groups[key].push_back(w);
    }
    vector<vector<string>> out;
    for (auto& [key, words] : groups) out.push_back(words);
    return out;
}

bool containsNearbyDuplicate(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
    unordered_set<int> window;                 // 最近 k 个数
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)nums.size(); i++) {
        if (window.count(nums[i])) return true;
        window.insert(nums[i]);
        if ((int)window.size() > k) window.erase(nums[i - k]);
    }
    return false;
}

struct PairHash {
    size_t operator()(const pair<int, int>& p) const {
        return hash<long long>()((long long)p.first << 32 | (unsigned)p.second);
    }
};

int main() {
    vector<int> a = {2, 7, 11, 15};
    auto r = twoSum(a, 9);
    cout << r[0] << ' ' << r[1] << '\n';

    vector<string> w = {"eat", "tea", "tan", "ate", "nat", "bat"};
    cout << groupAnagrams(w).size() << '\n';   // 3 组，组的顺序不确定

    vector<int> b = {1, 2, 3, 1};
    cout << containsNearbyDuplicate(b, 3) << containsNearbyDuplicate(b, 2) << '\n';

    unordered_set<pair<int, int>, PairHash> cells = {{0, 1}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}};
    cout << cells.size() << '\n';
}
```

```text
0 1
3
10
2
```

## 哈希表也会退化

所有键落进同一个桶时，每次操作都变成 O(n)。面试一般不会考到这一点，但有些竞赛会专门构造让 `unordered_map` 冲突的数据。预先知道元素个数时，`m.reserve(n)` 可以避免多次重新哈希。

## 常见错误

- 依赖 `unordered_map` 的遍历顺序。它在不同编译器、不同数据下都可能不一样，需要顺序就排序或者改用 `map`。
- 用 `[]` 查询，把不存在的键插了进去。
- 遍历时直接 `erase(it)` 然后 `++it`。`erase` 之后原迭代器失效，要写 `it = m.erase(it);`。
- 拿 `pair` 或 `vector` 当 `unordered_map` 的键，没提供哈希函数。

chapters.bodyEn:
`unordered_map` and `unordered_set` are hash tables: lookup, insert and erase are O(1) on average and O(n) at worst, and the elements have **no order**. Use them for counting, duplicate checks and "have I seen this"; when you need order, or a predecessor or successor, use the previous lesson's `set` and `map`.

## The basics

```cpp
unordered_map<int, int> cnt;
for (int x : nums) cnt[x]++;          // a missing key starts at 0
cnt.count(7);                          // 0 or 1
auto it = cnt.find(7);                 // when found, use it->first and it->second
if (it != cnt.end()) ...
cnt.erase(7);

unordered_set<string> seen;
seen.insert("a");
if (seen.count("a")) ...
```

`[]` inserts a default value, exactly as with `map`. Use `find` or `count` for lookups. `find` returns an iterator, so once found you can read `it->second` without a second lookup.

## map or unordered_map

| | `map` | `unordered_map` |
|---|---|---|
| Underneath | red-black tree | hash table |
| Lookup, insert | O(log n) | O(1) average, O(n) worst |
| Iteration order | sorted by key | unspecified |
| Key needs | comparison with `<` | a hash function |

Default to `unordered_map` in interviews. Use `map` when you need keys in order, need `lower_bound`, or the key is a type such as `pair` or `vector` that has no standard hash.

## pair as a key

The standard library has no hash for `pair`, so `unordered_set<pair<int, int>>` does not compile. Three ways out:

1. Use `set<pair<int, int>>` and pay a log factor.
2. Encode the two numbers as one integer, e.g. a grid cell as `r * cols + c`.
3. Write a hash function yourself (see the program below).

## Examples: two sum, grouping anagrams, nearby duplicates

```cpp run
#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <unordered_set>
#include <utility>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

vector<int> twoSum(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
    unordered_map<int, int> seen;              // value -> index
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)nums.size(); i++) {
        auto it = seen.find(target - nums[i]);
        if (it != seen.end()) return {it->second, i};
        seen[nums[i]] = i;
    }
    return {};
}

vector<vector<string>> groupAnagrams(vector<string>& strs) {
    unordered_map<string, vector<string>> groups;
    for (const string& w : strs) {
        string key = w;
        sort(key.begin(), key.end());          // the sorted letters are the key
        groups[key].push_back(w);
    }
    vector<vector<string>> out;
    for (auto& [key, words] : groups) out.push_back(words);
    return out;
}

bool containsNearbyDuplicate(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
    unordered_set<int> window;                 // the last k values
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)nums.size(); i++) {
        if (window.count(nums[i])) return true;
        window.insert(nums[i]);
        if ((int)window.size() > k) window.erase(nums[i - k]);
    }
    return false;
}

struct PairHash {
    size_t operator()(const pair<int, int>& p) const {
        return hash<long long>()((long long)p.first << 32 | (unsigned)p.second);
    }
};

int main() {
    vector<int> a = {2, 7, 11, 15};
    auto r = twoSum(a, 9);
    cout << r[0] << ' ' << r[1] << '\n';

    vector<string> w = {"eat", "tea", "tan", "ate", "nat", "bat"};
    cout << groupAnagrams(w).size() << '\n';   // 3 groups, in no particular order

    vector<int> b = {1, 2, 3, 1};
    cout << containsNearbyDuplicate(b, 3) << containsNearbyDuplicate(b, 2) << '\n';

    unordered_set<pair<int, int>, PairHash> cells = {{0, 1}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}};
    cout << cells.size() << '\n';
}
```

```text
0 1
3
10
2
```

## Hash tables can degrade

When every key lands in the same bucket, each operation becomes O(n). Interviews rarely go there, but some contests craft inputs that make `unordered_map` collide. When you know the number of elements in advance, `m.reserve(n)` avoids repeated rehashing.

## Common mistakes

- Relying on `unordered_map` iteration order. It can differ between compilers and inputs; sort, or use `map`, when order matters.
- Looking up with `[]` and inserting missing keys.
- Calling `erase(it)` and then `++it` in a loop. `erase` invalidates the iterator; write `it = m.erase(it);`.
- Using a `pair` or `vector` as an `unordered_map` key without a hash function.

chapters.bodyZh:
`<algorithm>` 里的 `sort`、`lower_bound` 这几个函数，在刷题时几乎每天都要用。这一课讲比较器的写法、排序稳定性，以及有序数组上的二分查找。

## sort

```cpp
sort(a.begin(), a.end());                    // 升序，O(n log n)
sort(a.begin(), a.end(), greater<int>());    // 降序
sort(a.rbegin(), a.rend());                  // 也是降序
sort(a.begin() + l, a.begin() + r);          // 只排 [l, r)
```

`vector<pair<int, int>>`、`vector<vector<int>>` 直接 `sort` 就按字典序排：先比第一个元素，相等再比第二个。

## 比较器必须是"严格小于"

自定义比较器 `cmp(a, b)` 的含义是"a 是否应该排在 b 前面"。它必须满足严格弱序：`cmp(a, a)` 必须是 `false`。

```cpp
sort(a.begin(), a.end(), [](int x, int y) { return x <= y; });   // 错！
```

用 `<=` 时 `cmp(a, a)` 为真，这是未定义行为：数据里有大量相等元素时，GCC 的 `sort` 可能越界读写，直接崩溃。永远用 `<` 或 `>`。多个关键字可以用 `tie` 比较，省得写一串 if：

```cpp
// 按分数降序，分数相同按名字升序
sort(v.begin(), v.end(), [](const Student& a, const Student& b) {
    return tie(b.score, a.name) < tie(a.score, b.name);
});
```

## 稳定性

`sort` **不稳定**：相等的元素排序后谁在前不确定。`stable_sort` 保证相等元素保持原来的相对顺序，复杂度同样是 O(n log n)。先按次要关键字排，再用 `stable_sort` 按主要关键字排，就得到"主要关键字相同时按次要关键字"的结果。

## 有序数组上的二分

```cpp
auto lo = lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), x);   // 第一个 >= x
auto hi = upper_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), x);   // 第一个 > x
int idx = lo - a.begin();                       // 转成下标
int cnt = hi - lo;                              // x 出现的次数
binary_search(a.begin(), a.end(), x);           // 只回答在不在
```

数组必须已经按同样的顺序排好。降序数组要传同样的比较器：`lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), x, greater<int>())`。

排序后去重是固定搭配：`unique` 把重复元素挪到末尾并返回新的结尾，再用 `erase` 删掉。

```cpp
sort(a.begin(), a.end());
a.erase(unique(a.begin(), a.end()), a.end());
```

## 例子：合并区间、最大数、搜索插入位置

合并区间按起点排序后扫一遍。"最大数"的比较器是这一课最经典的例子：两个数字串 a、b，`a + b > b + a` 时 a 排在前面。

```cpp run
#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

vector<vector<int>> merge(vector<vector<int>>& intervals) {
    sort(intervals.begin(), intervals.end());          // 按起点，再按终点
    vector<vector<int>> out;
    for (auto& iv : intervals) {
        if (!out.empty() && iv[0] <= out.back()[1])
            out.back()[1] = max(out.back()[1], iv[1]);   // 和上一个重叠：延长
        else
            out.push_back(iv);
    }
    return out;
}

string largestNumber(vector<int>& nums) {
    vector<string> s;
    for (int x : nums) s.push_back(to_string(x));
    sort(s.begin(), s.end(), [](const string& a, const string& b) { return a + b > b + a; });
    if (s[0] == "0") return "0";                        // 全是 0
    string out;
    for (auto& t : s) out += t;
    return out;
}

int searchInsert(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
    return lower_bound(nums.begin(), nums.end(), target) - nums.begin();
}

int main() {
    vector<vector<int>> iv = {{8, 10}, {1, 3}, {2, 6}, {15, 18}};
    auto m = merge(iv);
    for (size_t i = 0; i < m.size(); i++) cout << (i ? " " : "") << m[i][0] << '-' << m[i][1];
    cout << '\n';

    vector<int> nums = {3, 30, 34, 5, 9};
    cout << largestNumber(nums) << '\n';

    vector<int> sorted = {1, 3, 5, 6};
    cout << searchInsert(sorted, 5) << searchInsert(sorted, 2) << searchInsert(sorted, 7) << '\n';
}
```

```text
1-6 8-10 15-18
9534330
214
```

## 程序：lower_bound、stable_sort 和去重

```cpp run
#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <utility>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    vector<int> a = {1, 2, 2, 2, 5, 7};
    auto lo = lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), 2);
    auto hi = upper_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), 2);
    cout << lo - a.begin() << ' ' << hi - a.begin() << ' ' << hi - lo << '\n';
    cout << lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), 6) - a.begin() << '\n';   // 6 应插入的位置

    vector<pair<string, int>> people = {{"ann", 30}, {"bob", 25}, {"cat", 30}, {"dan", 25}};
    stable_sort(people.begin(), people.end(),
                [](const auto& x, const auto& y) { return x.second < y.second; });
    for (size_t i = 0; i < people.size(); i++) cout << (i ? " " : "") << people[i].first;
    cout << '\n';                                                     // 同龄人保持原顺序

    vector<int> b = {3, 1, 3, 2, 1};
    sort(b.begin(), b.end());
    b.erase(unique(b.begin(), b.end()), b.end());
    cout << b.size() << ": " << b[0] << b[1] << b[2] << '\n';
}
```

```text
1 4 3
5
bob dan ann cat
3: 123
```

## 常见错误

- 比较器写成 `<=`，在有很多相等元素的数据上崩溃。
- 以为 `sort` 是稳定的。需要稳定时用 `stable_sort`。
- 在没有排序的数组上用 `lower_bound`，或者数组降序却没传比较器。
- 只调用 `unique` 忘了 `erase`，数组长度不变，末尾留着垃圾值。

chapters.bodyEn:
`sort`, `lower_bound` and their neighbors in `<algorithm>` come up in almost every practice session. This lesson covers writing comparators, sort stability and binary search on sorted vectors.

## sort

```cpp
sort(a.begin(), a.end());                    // ascending, O(n log n)
sort(a.begin(), a.end(), greater<int>());    // descending
sort(a.rbegin(), a.rend());                  // also descending
sort(a.begin() + l, a.begin() + r);          // only [l, r)
```

A `vector<pair<int, int>>` or `vector<vector<int>>` sorts lexicographically with a plain `sort`: the first element, then the second on a tie.

## The comparator must be strictly "less than"

A custom comparator `cmp(a, b)` answers "should a come before b?". It must be a strict weak ordering, so `cmp(a, a)` must be `false`.

```cpp
sort(a.begin(), a.end(), [](int x, int y) { return x <= y; });   // wrong!
```

With `<=`, `cmp(a, a)` is true. That is undefined behavior: on data with many equal elements, GCC's `sort` can read and write out of bounds and crash. Always use `<` or `>`. For several keys, compare with `tie` instead of a chain of ifs:

```cpp
// score descending, then name ascending
sort(v.begin(), v.end(), [](const Student& a, const Student& b) {
    return tie(b.score, a.name) < tie(a.score, b.name);
});
```

## Stability

`sort` is **not stable**: equal elements can end up in any order. `stable_sort` keeps equal elements in their original order, still in O(n log n). Sort by the secondary key first, then `stable_sort` by the primary key, and ties on the primary key stay ordered by the secondary one.

## Binary search on a sorted vector

```cpp
auto lo = lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), x);   // the first >= x
auto hi = upper_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), x);   // the first > x
int idx = lo - a.begin();                       // as an index
int cnt = hi - lo;                              // how many times x occurs
binary_search(a.begin(), a.end(), x);           // just yes or no
```

The vector must already be sorted the same way. For a descending vector, pass the same comparator: `lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), x, greater<int>())`.

Sorting and then deduplicating is a fixed pair: `unique` moves the duplicates to the end and returns the new end, and `erase` removes them.

```cpp
sort(a.begin(), a.end());
a.erase(unique(a.begin(), a.end()), a.end());
```

## Examples: merge intervals, largest number, search insert position

Merging intervals is a sort by start and one pass. Largest Number has this lesson's classic comparator: for digit strings a and b, a goes first when `a + b > b + a`.

```cpp run
#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

vector<vector<int>> merge(vector<vector<int>>& intervals) {
    sort(intervals.begin(), intervals.end());          // by start, then end
    vector<vector<int>> out;
    for (auto& iv : intervals) {
        if (!out.empty() && iv[0] <= out.back()[1])
            out.back()[1] = max(out.back()[1], iv[1]);   // overlaps the last one: extend it
        else
            out.push_back(iv);
    }
    return out;
}

string largestNumber(vector<int>& nums) {
    vector<string> s;
    for (int x : nums) s.push_back(to_string(x));
    sort(s.begin(), s.end(), [](const string& a, const string& b) { return a + b > b + a; });
    if (s[0] == "0") return "0";                        // all zeros
    string out;
    for (auto& t : s) out += t;
    return out;
}

int searchInsert(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
    return lower_bound(nums.begin(), nums.end(), target) - nums.begin();
}

int main() {
    vector<vector<int>> iv = {{8, 10}, {1, 3}, {2, 6}, {15, 18}};
    auto m = merge(iv);
    for (size_t i = 0; i < m.size(); i++) cout << (i ? " " : "") << m[i][0] << '-' << m[i][1];
    cout << '\n';

    vector<int> nums = {3, 30, 34, 5, 9};
    cout << largestNumber(nums) << '\n';

    vector<int> sorted = {1, 3, 5, 6};
    cout << searchInsert(sorted, 5) << searchInsert(sorted, 2) << searchInsert(sorted, 7) << '\n';
}
```

```text
1-6 8-10 15-18
9534330
214
```

## A program: lower_bound, stable_sort and deduplication

```cpp run
#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <utility>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    vector<int> a = {1, 2, 2, 2, 5, 7};
    auto lo = lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), 2);
    auto hi = upper_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), 2);
    cout << lo - a.begin() << ' ' << hi - a.begin() << ' ' << hi - lo << '\n';
    cout << lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), 6) - a.begin() << '\n';   // where 6 would go

    vector<pair<string, int>> people = {{"ann", 30}, {"bob", 25}, {"cat", 30}, {"dan", 25}};
    stable_sort(people.begin(), people.end(),
                [](const auto& x, const auto& y) { return x.second < y.second; });
    for (size_t i = 0; i < people.size(); i++) cout << (i ? " " : "") << people[i].first;
    cout << '\n';                                                     // same age: original order

    vector<int> b = {3, 1, 3, 2, 1};
    sort(b.begin(), b.end());
    b.erase(unique(b.begin(), b.end()), b.end());
    cout << b.size() << ": " << b[0] << b[1] << b[2] << '\n';
}
```

```text
1 4 3
5
bob dan ann cat
3: 123
```

## Common mistakes

- A `<=` comparator that crashes on data with many equal elements.
- Assuming `sort` is stable. Use `stable_sort` when you need stability.
- Calling `lower_bound` on an unsorted vector, or on a descending one without the comparator.
- Calling `unique` without `erase`: the size stays the same and the tail holds leftovers.

chapters.bodyZh:
C++ 的整数有固定位数，溢出时不会报错，结果却已经错了。这一课集中讲整数溢出和几个只有 C++ 才有的坑。

## int 有多大

| 类型 | 位数 | 大约范围 |
|---|---|---|
| `int` | 32 | ±2.1×10⁹（`INT_MAX` = 2147483647） |
| `long long` | 64 | ±9.2×10¹⁸（`LLONG_MAX`） |

估算一下就知道 `int` 很容易不够用：10⁵ × 10⁵ = 10¹⁰，n = 10⁵ 个 10⁹ 相加是 10¹⁴。**有符号整数溢出是未定义行为**：不一定"绕回负数"，编译器优化后可能出现任何结果。

## 算之前就要是 long long

```cpp
int a = 100000, b = 100000;
long long bad = a * b;          // 先用 int 算乘法，已经溢出，再转成 long long 也救不回来
long long ok1 = 1LL * a * b;    // 先把一个操作数变成 long long
long long ok2 = (long long)a * b;
```

类似的地方：

- `accumulate(v.begin(), v.end(), 0)` 用 `int` 累加。初值写 `0LL`，累加才是 `long long`。
- `1 << 31` 超出了 `int`；位移超过 31 位要写 `1LL << k`。
- 二分的中点写 `lo + (hi - lo) / 2`，不写 `(lo + hi) / 2`。
- 比较 `mid * mid <= x` 时，`mid` 用 `long long`，或者改成 `mid <= x / mid`。
- `abs(INT_MIN)` 仍然溢出。

## 例子：x 的平方根

二分找最大的 m，使 m² ≤ x。x 最大是 2³¹ − 1，m² 用 `int` 计算会溢出，所以全程用 `long long`。

```cpp run
#include <climits>
#include <iostream>
#include <numeric>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

int mySqrt(int x) {
    long long lo = 0, hi = x;
    while (lo < hi) {
        long long mid = lo + (hi - lo + 1) / 2;   // 向上取中点，避免死循环
        if (mid * mid <= x) lo = mid;
        else hi = mid - 1;
    }
    return (int)lo;
}

int main() {
    cout << mySqrt(8) << ' ' << mySqrt(INT_MAX) << '\n';

    int a = 100000, b = 100000;
    cout << 1LL * a * b << '\n';

    vector<int> v = {2000000000, 2000000000};
    cout << accumulate(v.begin(), v.end(), 0LL) << '\n';

    cout << INT_MAX << ' ' << LLONG_MAX << '\n';
    cout << -7 / 2 << ' ' << -7 % 2 << '\n';      // 向零取整
}
```

```text
2 46340
10000000000
4000000000
2147483647 9223372036854775807
-3 -1
```

## 除法和取模向零取整

C++ 的 `/` 向零取整，`%` 的结果和被除数同号：`-7 / 2` 是 -3，`-7 % 2` 是 -1。Python 的 `-7 // 2` 是 -4，`-7 % 2` 是 1。要得到非负余数，写 `((x % m) + m) % m`。

## 其他只有 C++ 才有的坑

- **局部变量不会自动初始化。** `int sum;` 里是随机值，数组同理。写 `int sum = 0;`，或者用 `vector<int> a(n)`（会初始化为 0）。
- **`pow` 返回 `double`。** `(int)pow(10, 2)` 在某些平台上可能得到 99。整数的幂用循环自己乘。
- **`endl` 会刷新缓冲区。** 输出很多行时比 `'\n'` 慢得多。读入量大时，在 `main` 开头加 `ios::sync_with_stdio(false); cin.tie(nullptr);`。
- **有符号数和无符号数比较。** `-1 < v.size()` 的结果是 `false`：-1 先被转成巨大的无符号数。
- **返回局部变量的引用。** 函数返回后局部变量就销毁了，引用指向的内存已经无效。

## 常见错误

- 结果用 `long long` 存，中间的乘法还是 `int`。
- `accumulate` 的初值写成 `0`。
- 对负数取模，直接拿结果当数组下标。
- 输出几十万行时用 `endl`，导致超时。

chapters.bodyEn:
C++ integers have a fixed width, and overflow raises no error: the result is simply wrong. This lesson is about integer overflow and a few traps that only C++ has.

## How big is an int

| Type | Bits | Roughly |
|---|---|---|
| `int` | 32 | ±2.1×10⁹ (`INT_MAX` = 2147483647) |
| `long long` | 64 | ±9.2×10¹⁸ (`LLONG_MAX`) |

A quick estimate shows how easily `int` runs out: 10⁵ × 10⁵ = 10¹⁰, and 10⁵ values of 10⁹ add up to 10¹⁴. **Signed overflow is undefined behavior**: it does not reliably "wrap to a negative number", and after optimization anything can happen.

## Be long long before the arithmetic

```cpp
int a = 100000, b = 100000;
long long bad = a * b;          // multiplied as int, already overflowed; converting afterwards is too late
long long ok1 = 1LL * a * b;    // make one operand long long first
long long ok2 = (long long)a * b;
```

The same trap elsewhere:

- `accumulate(v.begin(), v.end(), 0)` sums in `int`. Start from `0LL` to sum in `long long`.
- `1 << 31` does not fit in an `int`; shifts past 31 bits need `1LL << k`.
- Write a binary search midpoint as `lo + (hi - lo) / 2`, not `(lo + hi) / 2`.
- When comparing `mid * mid <= x`, make `mid` a `long long`, or test `mid <= x / mid`.
- `abs(INT_MIN)` still overflows.

## Example: square root of x

Binary search for the largest m with m² ≤ x. x can be 2³¹ − 1, and m² overflows an `int`, so everything is `long long`.

```cpp run
#include <climits>
#include <iostream>
#include <numeric>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

int mySqrt(int x) {
    long long lo = 0, hi = x;
    while (lo < hi) {
        long long mid = lo + (hi - lo + 1) / 2;   // round up so the loop always shrinks
        if (mid * mid <= x) lo = mid;
        else hi = mid - 1;
    }
    return (int)lo;
}

int main() {
    cout << mySqrt(8) << ' ' << mySqrt(INT_MAX) << '\n';

    int a = 100000, b = 100000;
    cout << 1LL * a * b << '\n';

    vector<int> v = {2000000000, 2000000000};
    cout << accumulate(v.begin(), v.end(), 0LL) << '\n';

    cout << INT_MAX << ' ' << LLONG_MAX << '\n';
    cout << -7 / 2 << ' ' << -7 % 2 << '\n';      // truncates toward zero
}
```

```text
2 46340
10000000000
4000000000
2147483647 9223372036854775807
-3 -1
```

## Division and modulo truncate toward zero

C++ `/` truncates toward zero, and `%` takes the sign of the dividend: `-7 / 2` is -3 and `-7 % 2` is -1. In Python, `-7 // 2` is -4 and `-7 % 2` is 1. For a non-negative remainder, write `((x % m) + m) % m`.

## Other traps only C++ has

- **Locals are not initialized.** `int sum;` holds garbage, and so do plain arrays. Write `int sum = 0;`, or use `vector<int> a(n)`, which zero-fills.
- **`pow` returns a `double`.** `(int)pow(10, 2)` can come out as 99 on some platforms. Multiply in a loop for integer powers.
- **`endl` flushes the buffer.** Printing many lines with it is much slower than `'\n'`. For large input, start `main` with `ios::sync_with_stdio(false); cin.tie(nullptr);`.
- **Signed versus unsigned comparisons.** `-1 < v.size()` is `false`: -1 is converted to a huge unsigned number first.
- **Returning a reference to a local.** The local is destroyed when the function returns, so the reference points at dead memory.

## Common mistakes

- Storing the result in a `long long` while the multiplication is still done in `int`.
- Starting `accumulate` from `0`.
- Taking a negative number modulo m and using the result as an index.
- Printing hundreds of thousands of lines with `endl` and timing out.

chapters.bodyZh:
前面七课的要点压缩成几张表，面试前快速过一遍。复杂度里的 n 是容器当前的元素个数，"均摊"表示偶尔一次慢，平均下来仍是这个量级。

## 序列容器

| 容器 | 操作 | 复杂度 | 一行写法 |
|---|---|---|---|
| `vector` | 尾部追加 / 删除 | 均摊 O(1) / O(1) | `a.push_back(x); a.pop_back();` |
| `vector` | 下标访问 | O(1) | `a[i]`，调试时用 `a.at(i)` |
| `vector` | 中间插入 / 删除 | O(n) | `a.insert(a.begin() + i, x); a.erase(a.begin() + i);` |
| `vector` | 二维数组 | O(nm) | `vector<vector<int>> g(n, vector<int>(m));` |
| `string` | 追加字符 | 均摊 O(1) | `s += c;` |
| `string` | 子串 | O(len) | `s.substr(i, len)`（第二个参数是长度） |
| `string` | 查找 | 最坏 O(nm) | `s.find(t) != string::npos` |
| `deque` | 两端进出 | O(1) | `d.push_front(x); d.pop_back();` |
| `stack` | 入栈 / 看栈顶 / 出栈 | O(1) | `st.push(x); st.top(); st.pop();` |
| `queue` | 入队 / 看队头 / 出队 | O(1) | `q.push(x); q.front(); q.pop();` |

## 堆、有序容器、哈希容器

| 容器 | 操作 | 复杂度 | 一行写法 |
|---|---|---|---|
| `priority_queue` | 最大堆 push / pop | O(log n) | `priority_queue<int> pq;` |
| `priority_queue` | 最小堆 | O(log n) | `priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> pq;` |
| `priority_queue` | 用区间建堆 | O(n) | `priority_queue<int> pq(a.begin(), a.end());` |
| `set` | 插入 / 删除 / 查找 | O(log n) | `s.insert(x); s.erase(x); s.count(x);` |
| `set` | 最小 / 最大 | O(1) | `*s.begin(); *s.rbegin();` |
| `set` | 第一个 ≥ x / > x | O(log n) | `s.lower_bound(x); s.upper_bound(x);` |
| `multiset` | 只删一个 x | O(log n) | `ms.erase(ms.find(x));` |
| `map` | 计数 | O(log n) | `cnt[x]++;` |
| `map` | 按键有序遍历 | O(n) | `for (auto& [k, v] : m)` |
| `unordered_map` | 计数 / 查找 | 平均 O(1) | `cnt[x]++; m.find(k) != m.end();` |
| `unordered_set` | 判重 | 平均 O(1) | `if (!seen.insert(x).second) /* 重复 */;` |

## 算法

| 操作 | 复杂度 | 一行写法 |
|---|---|---|
| 排序 / 降序 | O(n log n) | `sort(a.begin(), a.end()); sort(a.rbegin(), a.rend());` |
| 稳定排序 | O(n log n) | `stable_sort(a.begin(), a.end(), cmp);` |
| 第一个 ≥ x 的下标 | O(log n) | `lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), x) - a.begin()` |
| x 出现的次数 | O(log n) | `upper_bound(...) - lower_bound(...)` |
| 排序后去重 | O(n) | `a.erase(unique(a.begin(), a.end()), a.end());` |
| 最大值 / 最小值 | O(n) | `*max_element(a.begin(), a.end())` |
| 求和 | O(n) | `accumulate(a.begin(), a.end(), 0LL)` |
| 反转 | O(n) | `reverse(a.begin(), a.end());` |
| 填 0, 1, 2, … | O(n) | `iota(a.begin(), a.end(), 0);` |
| 下一个排列 | O(n) | `next_permutation(a.begin(), a.end())` |

## 验证：表里的写法都能跑

```cpp run
#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <map>
#include <numeric>
#include <queue>
#include <set>
#include <string>
#include <unordered_set>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    vector<int> a = {4, 1, 3, 1, 2};
    cout << *max_element(a.begin(), a.end()) << ' ' << accumulate(a.begin(), a.end(), 0LL) << '\n';
    sort(a.begin(), a.end());
    cout << upper_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), 1) - lower_bound(a.begin(), a.end(), 1) << ' ';
    a.erase(unique(a.begin(), a.end()), a.end());
    cout << a.size() << '\n';

    vector<int> p(3);
    iota(p.begin(), p.end(), 1);              // 1 2 3
    int perms = 1;
    while (next_permutation(p.begin(), p.end())) perms++;
    cout << perms << '\n';

    unordered_set<int> seen;
    int dup = -1;
    for (int x : {5, 8, 5}) if (!seen.insert(x).second) dup = x;
    cout << dup << '\n';

    priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> pq(a.begin(), a.end());
    multiset<int> ms = {2, 2, 9};
    ms.erase(ms.find(2));
    map<char, int> cnt;
    for (char c : string("banana")) cnt[c]++;
    cout << pq.top() << ' ' << ms.size() << ' ' << cnt['a'] << ' ' << cnt.begin()->first << '\n';
}
```

```text
4 11
2 4
6
5
1 2 3 a
```

## 面试前最后检查一遍

- 乘法、累加会不会超过 2×10⁹？会就用 `long long`，而且在运算之前就转换。
- `a.size() - 1` 在空数组上会不会出问题？
- 比较器是不是严格的 `<` 或 `>`？
- 查询 `map` 时有没有误用 `[]`？
- 大容器是不是按引用传参？
- 输出很多行时，用的是 `'\n'` 还是 `endl`？

